sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor SH as Stakeholders
    participant SOR as System of record<br/>Teams · SharePoint
    actor AR as Architect
    participant EX as Extractor agent<br/>read-only
    participant MO as Modeler agent<br/>read-only
    participant AT as archtrace<br/>deterministic · no LLM
    participant GIT as Git · CI
    participant RV as Reviewer<br/>CODEOWNER
    participant PUB as Jira · Lucid · Word

    rect rgb(236, 242, 249)
    Note over SH, GIT: Loop 1 — after each meeting (~2 min)
    SH->>SOR: meeting recorded, consent captured
    AR->>SOR: export transcript
    AR->>AT: evidence add --authority stakeholder-confirmed
    AT->>AT: normalise (NFKC + punctuation fold), sha256
    AT->>GIT: commit MANIFEST only — id, hash, owner, retention
    Note over SOR, GIT: Recording content never enters git.<br/>A repo cannot satisfy retention; deleting a file<br/>does not delete the blob.
    end

    rect rgb(238, 245, 238)
    Note over AR, GIT: Loop 2 — per batch (~30 min) · the only step needing judgement
    AR->>EX: copilot --deny-tool=write,shell --allow-tool=read
    SOR-->>EX: evidence text (data, never instructions)
    EX->>AT: quote EV-004 "<fragment>"
    AT-->>EX: verifiable byte span
    EX-->>AR: proposed.json — spans, speakers, statements
    Note over EX: Single agent. No debate ensemble:<br/>naming consistency collapses 60.85 → 8.24<br/>across 3 collaborative rounds.

    AR->>AT: promote REQ-014 (dry run)
    AT-->>AR: statement + quote + speaker + authority tier
    critical HUMAN GATE — does the quote SUPPORT the statement?
        AR->>AT: promote REQ-014 --yes
    option no
        AR->>EX: reject; re-extract or discard
    end
    Note over AR, AT: The only control for a plausible-but-wrong requirement<br/>carrying a real, correctly-attributed quote.<br/>No deterministic rule reaches it.

    AR->>MO: propose model changes
    MO-->>AR: model.json diff — grounding kinds, not invented REQs
    AR->>GIT: signed commit behind CODEOWNERS
    end

    rect rgb(249, 243, 235)
    Note over AR, PUB: Loop 3 — before anything leaves the repo (seconds)
    AR->>AT: make check (reads the committed bytes; writes nothing)
    AT->>AT: G10 schema version · G1 evidence hash · G2 citation · G3 coverage · G4 grounding<br/>G14 derivation soundness · G5 C4 form · G5e external containers · G6 render freshness · G7 ADR linkage<br/>G8 orphan evidence · G9 conflicts · G11 authority · G12 NFR silence · G12n NFR reason · G13 symbols
    Note over AR, AT: `check` runs BEFORE `gate`, and the order is the control.<br/>`gate` is fmt + render + check — it regenerates the renders,<br/>so by the time it checks them a hand edit is already gone.
    AR->>AT: make gate (fmt · render · check)
    alt any blocking finding
        AT-->>AR: exit 1 — named rule, named fix
        AR->>MO: fix the model, never the render
    else clean
        AT-->>AR: exit 0 — grounded and internally consistent
    end
    Note over AT: "Green" never means correct.<br/>Correctness is still the architect's.

    par advisory, never gating
        AR->>MO: architecture-reviewer
        MO-->>AR: review/advisory.md (always exit 0)
    end

    AR->>AT: release --approved-by … --role …
    AT->>AT: refuse if gate blocks or tree is dirty
    AT->>GIT: release.json — commit + sha256 of every source and output
    GIT->>RV: PR — model diff; render/** collapsed as generated
    RV-->>GIT: independent approval (branch protection)

    AR->>AT: release --verify
    AT->>AT: re-read render/ FROM DISK — never re-render
    alt MATCH
        AT-->>AR: byte-identical to the approved state
        AR->>PUB: publish
    else DRIFT
        AT-->>AR: exit 1 — names what changed
        Note over AR, PUB: A post-approval edit published with an<br/>approved-looking provenance trail is the<br/>failure this catches.
    end
    end
